# Client figure selection

A listen-server client must pick its own figures from
portraits, a world click, and keys 1-4. HUD and
replication edits keep breaking this. Check the
client path, not only the host.

## Canvas overlays

`AddChildToCanvas` stretch-fills the HUD. That covers
`HB_LocalFigures`. Portraits get no click. `HitsHud`
then eats world clicks too.

```cpp
// Fills the HUD. Portraits die.
Canvas->AddChildToCanvas(Box);

UCanvasPanelSlot* Slot =
	Canvas->AddChildToCanvas(Box);
Slot->SetAnchors(FAnchors(0.5f, 1.f));
Slot->SetAutoSize(true);
```

Set AutoSize in the same function as the add.
`Place*` can return before Slate has a size.
Empty Jump/Fall/action rows stay `Collapsed`.

## HitsHud

Test portraits and buttons only. Never a stretch
row (`HB_LocalFigures`, `HB_ActionButtons`).
Skip `Collapsed`, `Hidden`, `HitTestInvisible`,
`SelfHitTestInvisible`, and size under 1.
The Play widget itself is `SelfHitTestInvisible`.
`JoA.Match.TwoPlayerFlow` CheckPortraitHits must
keep the board centre free of HUD hits.

## OwnsFigure

`OwningPlayerState` can still be unmapped. Match
`SeatIndex` to `OwningPlayerIndex`. `SyncFigures`
waits until one of those is known. Do not leave an
own figure in `HB_OpponentFigures` or with
`SetClickable(false)`.

`OnRep_SeatIndex` on the player state and
`OnRep_OwningPlayerIndex` on the figure must both
`NotifyBoardChanged`. The seat int often arrives
after the first HUD build. Team tint in
`OnRep_OwningPlayerIndex` is not enough.

## Test

`JoA.Match.TwoPlayerFlow` CheckPortraitHits. Own-row
portraits on `NM_Client` must be `Visible`.
